# draftstep.part -- Rounds of a drafted block where a plate steps back
# Copyright (c) 2026 Jakob Kastelic

# A block 40 x 20 drafted 3 deg along y, and across it a plate whose
# front, seen from the side, steps back sharply: at y = -20 from z = -15
# to 5, then back to y = -10 above, with no arc at the steps.  The edge
# where the drafted sides of the block meet the plate gets a round of 1.
profile b along y -20 -10 0 20 -10 0 20 10 0 -20 10 0
extrude box from 0 to -30 b draft 3
profile w along x 5 -15 0 5 15 0 -10 15 0 -10 5 0 -20 5 0 -20 -15 0
extrude plate from -25 to 25 w
common part box plate
round 1 box.side plate
